Here's an example Java code that incorporates the formula EI = (E + R + M) / 3 to create an interactive storytelling activity for toddlers:
```
import java.util.Scanner;
public class StorytellingActivity {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner input = new Scanner(System.in);

        // Define variables for empathy, resilience, and mindfulness
        int empathy = 0;
        int resilience = 0;
        int mindfulness = 0;

        // Generate a story with interactive elements
        System.out.println("Once upon a time, there was a little rabbit named Rosie.");
        System.out.println("Rosie loved to play outside and explore the world around her.");
        System.out.println("One day, while she was hopping through the forest, she saw a squirrel who looked very sad.");
        System.out.println("What do you think Rosie should do?");
        System.out.println("1. Ignore the squirrel and keep hopping.");
        System.out.println("2. Go up to the squirrel and ask if everything is okay.");
        int choice = input.nextInt();

        if (choice == 1) {
            System.out.println("Rosie continued hopping and didn't notice the squirrel's sadness.");
            resilience++;
        } else if (choice == 2) {
            System.out.println("Rosie went up to the squirrel and asked if everything was okay.");
            System.out.println("The squirrel told Rosie that he had lost his acorn and was feeling very upset.");
            empathy++;
            mindfulness++;
        }

        // Calculate the emotional intelligence score
        double ei = (double) (empathy + resilience + mindfulness) / 3;
        System.out.println("Your emotional intelligence score is " + ei);

        // Provide prompts for discussions with children
        System.out.println("Let's talk about how Rosie showed empathy, resilience, and mindfulness in this story.");
        System.out.println("How do you feel when you see someone who is sad or upset?");
        System.out.println("What can you do to help them feel better?");
        System.out.println("How do you handle difficult situations when things don't go as planned?");
        System.out.println("What are some ways you can practice mindfulness in your daily life?");
    }
}
```
This code generates a simple story about a rabbit and a squirrel and prompts the user to make a choice that reflects empathy, resilience, and mindfulness. The code then calculates the emotional intelligence score using the formula EI = (E + R + M) / 3 and provides prompts for discussions with children.

